//MCQ

::DataFrame Definition::
What is a DataFrame in Spark?
{
    ~ A single-node in-memory collection
    = A distributed collection of data organized into named columns
    ~ A replacement for SparkSession
    ~ A file format like Parquet
}

::Creating DataFrame::
Which of the following is a valid way to create a DataFrame in PySpark?
{
    ~ spark.createRDD(data)
    = spark.createDataFrame(data, columns)
    ~ sc.createDataFrame(data)
    ~ DataFrame(data)
}

::DataFrame Transformation::
Which operation is considered a transformation on a DataFrame?
{
    = filter()
    ~ show()
    ~ collect()
    ~ count()
}
